    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51747.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "So I think I'm uniquely focusing on what I think the central issue this country faces, which is how terribly divided we are. We have a divider and chief in the White House. I think the next president needs to try to bring this country together, which doesn't mean we're going to agree with each other on everything. But just to restore this notion of common purpose that we're all in it together, and we got to work hard to leave the world better than we found it. So that's one thing. I'm also a problem solver, because as I said, my background is very different. And I just think I have new ideas on all the big issues we face, whether it be health care or climate, go down the list. I think I have really new ideas.",
