    "turn_text": "So there's two issues with that that I'm worried about. I want to give it to the issues in a second. But as a structural matter, I'm worried that that's not really how it works. That the Republican Party is specific, but unfortunately a lot of the Democratic Party too takes a giant amount of donations. And then when they take those corporate donations, etc. You're not going to be able to convince them. There is no beer summit that will talk Mitch McConnell out of supporting his corporate donors. So I worry that that's a misunderstanding of how they make decisions, especially in the Republican",
